{"summary":"Reject the claimed compile-fix amendment because the cited syntax error is not present and `cargo check -p tank_core` succeeds. Accept the remaining amendments: they identify a dead egg-drop parameter and a real egg-drop regression, a missing molt-stress term in snapshot diagnostics, an unused `HighDensity` event cause, and two deterministic test failures in `reproduction_factors`.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-5-1cf2cbc3","decision":"reject","rationale":"The current `egg_dropping()` body has balanced braces, `causes` is still in scope at the emit call, and `cargo check -p tank_core` passes. This amendment describes a syntax error that is not present in the code under review."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-c0817a06","decision":"accept","rationale":"`egg_drop_temp_swing_c` is defined, defaulted, serialized, and asserted in tests, but runtime logic no longer reads it. That leaves a dead configuration knob and stale documentation/comments, so it should either be removed end-to-end or restored to the egg-dropping logic."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-52f42a9a","decision":"accept","rationale":"`update_reproductive_readiness()` includes `f_molt`, but `dominant_repro_suppression()` omits it while claiming to mirror the shrimp-system factors. When molt stress is the strongest suppressor, the snapshot will report the wrong cause, so this is a real diagnostic-correctness bug."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-3d54a6d2","decision":"accept","rationale":"`EventCause::HighDensity` is currently dead: it is defined but never emitted. That is unnecessary API surface and inconsistent instrumentation; either emit it from a real density-suppression path or remove it."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-82009a69","decision":"accept","rationale":"The regression is real. `egg_dropping()` now only checks `instability_index`, while `update_stability_tracker()` moves that index only 30% toward the day's raw instability. From a stable baseline, even a very large same-day swing tops out at `0.3`, below the default `0.5` threshold, so first-day shock egg drops are effectively disabled."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-98b094a7","decision":"accept","rationale":"This is a concrete failing-test regression. Zeroing `shrimp_periphyton_grazing_g_per_shrimp_per_day` makes `shrimp_target_food_route_g()` return `0.0`, and `update_condition()` treats that as fully satiated (`food_factor = 1.0`), so the intended 'starved' tank becomes healthier than the fed tank. `cargo test -p tank_core --test reproduction_factors` fails exactly as described."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-7f760efe","decision":"accept","rationale":"This test still fails deterministically in the current tree: `cargo test -p tank_core --test reproduction_factors` reports `test_mature_stable_tank_breeds_well` failing because only one `ShrimpBerried` event occurs. Whether the scenario needs retuning or the assertion needs adjustment, the amendment correctly identifies a real breakage that must be resolved."}]}